%[text] %[text:anchor:H_68CCA533] ### **a. Magnitude of Force Vector** 
%[text]{"align":"center"} If $\\vec{F} =\\left(F\_x \\hat{i} +F\_y \\hat{j} +F\_z \\hat{k} \\right)${"editStyle":"visual"} , Then $F\_r =\\left|\\vec{F} \\right|=\\sqrt{F\_x^2 +F\_y^2 +F\_z^2 }${"editStyle":"visual"} 
%[text] **Problem Description:**  For components $F\_x${"editStyle":"visual"} , $F\_y${"editStyle":"visual"} , and $F\_z${"editStyle":"visual"} of force vector $\\vec{F}$ , write a program that 
%[text] 1. describes the force in vector form and stores it in variable `F`
%[text] 2. find its magnitude and assign it to variable `F_r` \
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_7FC45914] Substitute `Fx` , `Fy` and `Fz` as `2` , `3` and `4` , respectively to find `F_r` using your program. Assign it to variable `A`. 
%[text] **Graded Exercise:**  After implementing this in MATLAB Grader, students will use an exercise like the following: 
